+For an active coordinated assignment, the version 2 peer inventory also freezes its assignment and exact original source incorporation, consumer regression and combined verification selectors. The verifier reads those original current accepted records under the explicit session contexts. Each consumer regression follows incorporation at the affected repository head; a separate accepted quality, API or UAT verification freezes a mandatory integrated criterion and the actual head tuple containing every producer and consumer contribution. Unrelated repository boundaries retain the normal peer proof requirements. The executable owner of these checks and automatic dependency readiness is scripts/workflow-coordination.mjs, under resources/orchestrator.json#workflowTopologies.coordination.
+
+The report retains each source consumer's sealed incorporation intent and actual merge receipt. Combined proof additionally joins actual API and browser endpoint records to two accepted runtime observations per role, bracketing each verifier. Those observations measure the serving checkout and process; pinned source contexts cannot substitute for served heads. A BE-only extraction still requires the consumers' delivered FE contributions in the combined runtime when their original missions include FE, without inventing an FE source application for the BE producer. The authoritative selectors are the existing request integration and peer/report schemas; `scripts/workflow-runtime-proof.mjs` verifies their measured joins.
+
 ---
 
 Source: [`operators/workflow-verify/operator.md`](https://github.com/starci183/starci-skills/blob/main/operators/workflow-verify/operator.md).
